+# Proposed Windows CUDA runtime producer contract
+
+New GPU producer only; existing CPU recipe/source/receipts remain untouched. One static ORT1.30.0 core at upstream f2c39fe2f838cf35ce7da92824f5a5e3ee6e88a7, plus same-build optional shared providers. New source identity frames exact original source inventory, reviewed loader/offline patches, original16dependency archives and transformed frontend source; no CPU qualification or release authority.
+
+Preparation must reuse canonical CPU-owner path/archive/hash/tool/owned-process functions without changing CPU globals or pretending the GPU source matches the original CPU verify_build result. Copy/extract original verified source into fresh protected same-human output. Apply exact reviewed source changes only after before-SHA matching; require exact after-SHAs and full final source census. All16dependency archives are available offline and pinned SHA256 plus upstream deps.txt SHA1. CMake FetchContent declarations refuse nonlocal/missing URLs. Frontend is explicitly pre-extracted with only its authenticated9-byte .claude/skills symlink omitted; never follow/create it. Retain raw archive/full census and exclusion record. The original upstream dynamic-loading patch fails against its declared1.27 source; retain its original hash and exact failed context as history, do not run it. Apply the pinned upstream ARM64 compatibility patch and the explicit reviewed rebased Windows shim patch (validate full before/after bytes). The Windows imported-module-only helper: driver/cudart handles may be referenced only after authenticated native preloading, without environment override or a fresh lookup. Non-Windows behavior remains out of scope and unchanged. CUTLASS's own reviewed upstream patch remains part of CMake's local-archive population.
+
+The new owner prepares fresh inputs and exact configure/build cards; actual configure/build requires Root-reviewed frozen script/lock, explicit --execute-build and single ownership. Both stages share one monotonic wall budget <=10800seconds, use existing canonical suspended-owned-job runner and retain first failure/actual settlement. No automatic retry/resume or old output overwrite. Exactsource/toolkit/dependency/dev inputs are rechecked after stages. A failure leaves build state/logs/partial receipt. Static libraries and provider DLLs are only producer outputs, not admitted payloads. No Cargo environment/publication/qualification is emitted by this new owner yet; subsequent GPU aggregate/runtime/package consumers require the new producer proof rather than CPU acceptance bypasses.
+
+Before model work: actual image imports must establish no eager CUDA/provider dependency in service, no second ORT core and inference-free CLI; runtime auth/protected layout/loaded-module checks and narrowed DLL policy must exist; CPU-without-GPU-deps refusal controls and tiny native provider placement must pass. Strict FP32/TF32off uses unchanged unfused graph and native tensors. Neither this script nor its build receipt calls a model or signs a qualification decision. Retain full NVIDIA/ORT/CUTLASS/frontend/third-party notices; proprietary runtimes stay independently licensed. Actual archivedcuDNN LICENSE takes precedence over mutable metadata copies.
