+# GPU producer R2 review handoff
+
+Actual: the approved two OS negative controls passed once (0.070465s), with no valid module loaded. cuDNN683336095-byte official archive passed SHA/preflight in49.525s; safe extraction of8DLL/7headers/16importlibs+LICENSE passed8.182s. Cutlass4.7.0 and frontend1.27.0 source archives match the existing upstream SHA1 and now have retained SHA256/inert censuses/notices. Originals and new protected output ACLs are preserved. No C++/Cargo/model/install/GPUprovider execution has occurred.
+
+Active new producer is provision_cuda_runtime.py plus cuda-runtime-producer-lock.json, CONTRACT.md, offline-helper.patch and frontend-authenticated-imports.patch in this R2 folder; it also consumes the unchanged approved loader R2 patch one level above. Histories before-self-review/failed-r1 are inactive and retained. Private records/scripts are not a new public native wire protocol or qualification proof. Existing CPU files/receipts remain unmodified.
+
+The unmodified upstream frontend dynamic-loader patch does not apply to declared1.27 source (its third hunk predates the environment-override block). R1 preparation failed before a build; R2 explicitly rebases the Windows helpers to reference only authenticated preloaded nvcuda/cudart12 modules and retains the original nonWindows bodies. It keeps upstream direct-call CUDA macros and separately applies the exact upstream ARM64 compatibility patch. It does not run fuzzy patching or downgrade a dependency. One inert .claude/skills link is recorded/omitted; no link is extracted or followed.
+
+Six Python helper/refusal controls pass on the frozen producer. An initial5/6 result was a test-only Windows path separator expectation; failure/source are retained. Current controls cover exact F32 single-core configure decisions, CPUrecipe drift, permitted nonbuild-link omission, unexpected-link refusal, traversal refusal and archive-hash drift. They do not establish C++ compilation, frontend/cuDNN ABI compatibility, final static linking or any GPU/model outcome. The producer's first /Zs header syntax stage is before full configure/build, so that compatibility failure stops cheaply.
+
+build-card-r2.json provides a concrete unexecuted command and actual inputs. Root must review the producer and patches before execution. The eventual aggregate/runtime/build/package consumers still need a new GPU proof owner; do not pass this receipt through existing CPU-only verify_build or infer native model qualification. Use original FP32 unfused Compact/Large graphs and TF32off only. No F16/BF16/mixed/Flash graph work is in scope. Missing GPU dependencies must preserve MiniLM CPU and separately qualified same-slot CPU fallback; Large currently has no qualified CPU fallback.
